Chapter: BitopIfCond
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A codegen regression. A bit operation in an `if` CONDITION inside a
 frameless tail loop. `bit-and x 1` reaches the plug as a curried
 IrApply, so `rv-emit-direct-call` found the bitwise runtime helper by
 name and emitted a `jal` to it BEFORE its own inline arm -- fatal in a
 frameless function, where the call clobbers ra, the argument registers
 and the parameters, so the loop hung with zero output. The fix skips
 the helper for an inline builtin at its own arity, so `bit-and x 1`
 lowers to `and` inline. count-ones 5 = 2 (101), 255 = 8, and count-nz
 (the same shape with division instead of a bit op) sits beside it.

Section: Loop

  count-ones : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  count-ones (x) (acc) =
   if x == 0 then acc
   else if bit-and x 1 == 1 then count-ones (bit-shru x 1) (acc + 1)
    else count-ones (bit-shru x 1) acc

  count-nz : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  count-nz (x) (acc) =
   if x == 0 then acc
   else if x - (x / 2) * 2 == 1 then count-nz (x / 2) (acc + 1)
    else count-nz (x / 2) acc

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("count-ones 5: " & show (count-ones 5 0))
    print-line-uni ("count-ones 255: " & show (count-ones 255 0))
    print-line-uni ("count-nz 5: " & show (count-nz 5 0))
  end
